From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:23:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: hevc: Apply the request controls before
 reading them

rkvdec_hevc_run_preamble() looks up the HEVC controls and stores their
p_cur pointers, the slice count and the SPS RPS pointers first, and only
then calls rkvdec_run_preamble(), which applies the request's controls
with v4l2_ctrl_request_setup().

For the fixed-size compound controls this happens to work: p_cur points
to storage that stays in place, and its contents are updated by the
setup before the codec code reads them. It is wrong for the rest:

- SLICE_PARAMS, EXT_SPS_ST_RPS and EXT_SPS_LT_RPS are dynamic arrays.
  When a request holds more elements than the control has room for,
  req_to_new() allocates a new p_array and frees the old one, so the
  pointer read before the setup is left dangling for that job.
- num_slices is taken from new_elems before the setup. That is the
  count last stored there: of the previous request, or of a later one
  whose controls userspace has already set. The RK3399 HEVC backend
  programs it into the hardware and walks that many slice parameters.
- ext_sps_st_rps/ext_sps_lt_rps are chosen from has_sps_st_rps and
  has_sps_lt_rps, which rkvdec_s_ctrl() sets while the request is
  applied. On the first request that carries the controls the pointers
  are therefore NULL and the RPS table isn't built for that job.

Apply the request first, as cedrus and hantro do, then read the
controls.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c  | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c
index 2b8e04dd1..f581212fc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c
@@ -429,6 +429,13 @@ void rkvdec_hevc_run_preamble(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx,
 {
 	struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl;
 
+	/*
+	 * Apply the request's controls first: they are only copied to the
+	 * current values here, and a dynamic array control may get a new
+	 * p_cur buffer when the request holds more elements than before.
+	 */
+	rkvdec_run_preamble(ctx, &run->base);
+
 	ctrl = v4l2_ctrl_find(&ctx->ctrl_hdl,
 			      V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_DECODE_PARAMS);
 	run->decode_params = ctrl ? ctrl->p_cur.p : NULL;
@@ -460,6 +467,4 @@ void rkvdec_hevc_run_preamble(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx,
 	} else {
 		run->ext_sps_lt_rps = NULL;
 	}
-
-	rkvdec_run_preamble(ctx, &run->base);
 }
